 {
  "name": "Smoky Lentil Chili with Squash",
  "category": "Vegetarian",
  "source_id": "52784",
  "instructions_excerpt": "Add the remaining spices – paprika, cinnamon, chilli, cocoa, Worcestershire sauce, salt, and oregano. Next add the can of tomatoes, the water or stock, and carrots. Serve with sliced jalapeno, lime wedges, cilantro, green onions, and cashew sour cream. SIMPLE CASHEW SOUR CREAM 1 Cup Raw Unsalted Cashews Apple Cider Vinegar Bring some water to the boil, and use it to soak the cashews for at least four hours. Alternatively, you can use cold water and let the cashews soak overnight, but I’m forgetful/lazy, so often use the boil method which is much faster. After the cashews have soaked, drain them and add to a high speed blender.",
