 {
  "name": "Sushi",
  "category": "Seafood",
  "source_id": "53065",
  "instructions_excerpt": "Spread over some Japanese mayonnaise. Use a spoon to spread out a thin layer of mayonnaise down the middle of the rice. Get your child to top the mayonnaise with a line of their favourite fillings – here we’ve used tuna and cucumber. TO MAKE PRESSED SUSHI: Layer over some smoked salmon. Line a loaf tin with cling film, then place a thin layer of smoked salmon inside on top of the cling film. Press about 3cm of rice over the fish, fold the cling film over and press down as much as you can, using another tin if you have one. Get a small square of cling film and place a topping, like half a prawn or a small piece of smoked salmon, on it.",
